# DEPLOY PERSONAL DEVELOPER VERSIONS OF AWS VIZ-PIPELINE RESOURCES

1. Edit the configuration.yml file adjacent to this README. There are inline notes to help.
2. Right click this file on the left and select "Open in Integrated Terminal
3. Execute `aws sso login --profile <profile_name>` to log into your AWS account via the command line
4. Execute `terraform init` (like `git init` this should only be needed this one time and never again)
5. Execute `terraform apply` (this is the command you'll keep coming back to when deploying code updates)
6. Type `yes` if you'd like to accept the plan, or `no` if something doesn't look right.

If you accept the plan, the resources set to `true` in the `deploy_resources` section will be created for you. 
Any lambdas you create will be referenced by your own viz-pipeline step function. Otherwise, your step function 
will reference the official "-ti-" resources.

From here, you can make changes to your resources via the AWS GUI or via code. Just note that any changes made directly 
via the GUI will be overwritten the next time you run `terraform apply` if they were not reflected back into the code base.